{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788200598,"nonce":"ycleFZ9ZnvvnIdDW6wEHnvslSsA=","message":"VERIFICATION (backlog verification pass, git-bug 2f2796e, run fbb2c59)\n\nCONFIRMED — with four material additions, one of which changes the fix.\n\nWHAT I CONFIRMED BY READING\n\n1. `ThingPlaceMode.Near` slides and returns true. `Verse/GenPlace.TryPlaceThing`\n   (the `out Thing lastResultingThing` overload), `mode == ThingPlaceMode.Near`\n   branch: it calls `TryFindPlaceSpotNear`, then `TryPlaceDirect(thing, bestSpot, ...)`\n   and `return true`. `bestSpot` is whatever cell won the search — the requested\n   `center` has no privileged status once a better-scoring cell exists.\n2. The mod does exactly what the issue says. `Source/AutoRimmer/DevVerbs.cs`,\n   `DevVerbs.SpawnThing`: `mode` defaults to `\"near\"`, and the non-building path is\n   `GenPlace.TryPlaceThing(thing, target, map, mode == \"direct\" ? Direct : Near, out result)`.\n   `data[\"at\"]` is `Positions.Out(target)` (requested) and `data[\"spawned\"]` is\n   `Dev.Describe(result)` (actual). Nothing compares them. CONFIRMED.\n3. The \"what already works\" paragraph is accurate, member by member:\n   `failures.Add({at, reason, blocker})` with `Blockers.Describe`; `if (!ok) break;`;\n   `[\"requested\"] = count` beside `[\"placed\"] = placed`; and the\n   `GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt(def, target, map, thing.Rotation, canWipeEdifices: true)`\n   pre-check on the building branch. All present. CONFIRMED.\n4. `dev:spawn-pawn` is a second site. CONFIRMED — `DevVerbs.SpawnPawn`:\n   `if (!cell.Standable(map)) cell = CellFinder.RandomClosewalkCellNear(at, map, Math.Max(3, spread));`\n   then `GenSpawn.Spawn(pawn, cell, map)`. Same silent-slide shape, and it also\n   burns the shared `Rand` stream on the fallback.\n\nADDITION 1 — THE SLIDE IS NOT BOUNDED TO ONE CELL, AND THE ISSUE SHOULD NOT BE\nREAD AS IF IT WERE. Both measurements were one cell; the mechanism is not.\n`GenPlace.TryFindPlaceSpotNear` scans three widening rings — `RadialPattern[0..8]`,\nthen `PlaceNearMiddleRadialCells` (`GenRadial.NumCellsInRadius(3f)`), then\n`PlaceNearMaxRadialCells` (`GenRadial.NumCellsInRadius(12.9f)`) — and accepts any\ncell scoring above `PlaceSpotQuality.Unusable` on the last pass. **A thing can\nlegally land ~12.9 cells from where it was asked for and still report `ok:true`.**\nIt can also land in a DIFFERENT ROOM: `PlaceSpotQualityAt` grades a\ndifferent-room cell `Bad` (or `Awful` if unreachable) rather than `Unusable`. For\n3.3 that is the difference between \"the wall is one off\" and \"the wall is in the\nnext building\".\n\nADDITION 2 — **`mode:\"direct\"` IS NOT AN EXACT-OR-REFUSE MODE. Do not implement\n`exact:true` by routing to it.** This is the one that would have cost a round\ntrip. `GenPlace.TryPlaceDirect` performs no spawnability check whatsoever: after\nthe stack-absorb loop it calls `SplitAndSpawnOneStackOnCell` -\u003e `GenSpawn.Spawn(thing2, loc, map, rot)`\nunconditionally. For an item it refuses only incidentally, via\n`num3 = loc.GetMaxItemsAllowedInCell(map) - (item count at loc)` reaching `\u003c= 0`\n— i.e. it refuses a cell that is full OF ITEMS and places straight on top of a\nbed, a table or a wall. For anything with `stackLimit \u003c= 1` even that is\noverridden (`if (num3 \u003c= 0 \u0026\u0026 thing.def.stackLimit \u003c= 1) num3 = 1;`).\n\nTHE CLEAN IMPLEMENTATION, and it is already in the signature the mod calls:\n`GenPlace.TryPlaceThing` takes a `Predicate\u003cIntVec3\u003e extraValidator`, which\n`TryFindPlaceSpotNear` passes to `PlaceSpotQualityAt`, which returns `Unusable`\nfor any cell the predicate rejects. So\n\n    GenPlace.TryPlaceThing(thing, target, map, ThingPlaceMode.Near, out result,\n                           null, (IntVec3 c) =\u003e c == target, rot)\n\nis exact-or-refuse **using the game own placement grading**, and returns false\nrather than sliding. That is strictly better than a hand-rolled pre-check,\nbecause it inherits `CanSpawnAt`, the item-count cap, `IHaulDestination.Accepts`\nand the stack rules for free. Recommended.\n\nADDITION 3 — THERE IS A THIRD SILENT-MUTATION SHAPE IN THE SAME VERB AND IT IS\nWORSE THAN A SLIDE: A WIPE. `mode:\"direct\"` on a `ThingCategory.Building` runs\n`GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt(..., canWipeEdifices: true)` and then\n`GenSpawn.Spawn(thing, target, map, rot, WipeMode.VanishOrMoveAside)`. In\n`Verse/GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt`, the edifice test is `if (!canWipeEdifices \u0026\u0026 map.edificeGrid[item] != null) return false;`\n— passing `true` **disables it**, so an occupied cell passes the pre-check. Then\n`GenSpawn.Spawn` case `WipeMode.VanishOrMoveAside` runs `CheckMoveItemsAside`\n(which DeSpawns loose items and re-places them `Near`, or `Destroy()`s them if\nthat fails) followed by `WipeExistingThings(..., DestroyMode.Vanish)`, which\ndestroys everything `GenSpawn.SpawningWipes` says the new def wipes. So today\n`dev:spawn-thing {def:\"Wall\", mode:\"direct\"}` onto an occupied cell reports plain\nsuccess and silently DELETES what was there. Same class of bug as the slide, and\nthe exact-or-refuse default should cover it: for a building, the default must\nalso refuse when `GenSpawn.WouldWipeAnythingWith(target, rot, def, map, t =\u003e true)`\nholds, with the opt-in named separately from `near` (they are different\npermissions: \"put it nearby\" vs \"destroy what is there\").\n\nADDITION 4 — A `Log.Error` PATH THE ISSUE DOES NOT MENTION, RELEVANT TO\nZERO-RED-ERRORS. The `Near` branch of `GenPlace.TryPlaceThing` ends its\ndo/while with `Log.Error(\"Failed to place \" + thing + \" at \" + center + \" in mode \" + mode + \".\")`\nwhen `TryFindPlaceSpotNear` SUCCEEDED but `TryPlaceDirect` then failed without\nconsuming any of the stack. It is reachable (a spot graded usable whose cell\nthen refuses the item), so the `Near` path is not red-error-free either, and the\nissue reads as though only the building path was.\n\nNOTES ON THE ACCEPTANCE — testable, with two words that need pinning\n\n- \"Spawning onto an OCCUPIED cell with the default settings REFUSES\" needs\n  \"occupied\" replaced by the criterion that actually matters, which is\n  `result.Position != requested`. Placing 75 steel onto a cell holding 40 steel\n  is `PlaceSpotQuality.Perfect`, stacks in place, lands at the exact cell, and\n  MUST NOT refuse — `PlaceSpotQualityAt` returns `Perfect` on\n  `thing3.CanStackWith(thing) \u0026\u0026 thing3.stackCount \u003c stackLimit`. Written as\n  \"occupied\", a literal implementation breaks stacking, which is how every\n  `stockpile:` call arrives.\n- The blocker report needs a wider lookup than the one in the file today. The\n  existing failure path uses `Blockers.Describe(target.GetFirstBuilding(map))`,\n  which is `null` when the obstruction is an item, a plant or a pawn — and the\n  issue own reproduction #2 (a steel stack refused a cell) is exactly that case.\n  Use the thing list at the cell, not `GetFirstBuilding`.\n- `Blockers.Describe` already returns `removal` as a key of its own dictionary,\n  so \"the blocker (via Blockers.Describe) AND its removal value\" is one field,\n  not two. No work implied; noting it so nobody adds a duplicate key.\n- The live reproduction lines are reproducible as written and are the right\n  acceptance. They need the bench (orchestrator-run): `dev:spawn-thing {def:\"Bed\",\n  stuff:\"WoodLog\", pos:[112,108]}` twice, and `dev:spawn-thing {def:\"Steel\",\n  count:75, pos:[100,113]}` onto the occupied cell.\n\nCOMPLETE `GenPlace`/`GenSpawn` CALL-SITE INVENTORY (for the closing comment the\nacceptance asks for — this is the audit, done, so the worker can spend its\nbudget on the fix):\n\n  DevVerbs.SpawnThing            GenPlace.TryPlaceThing Near|Direct   SLIDES / WIPES — the subject of this issue\n  DevVerbs.SpawnThing (building) GenSpawn.Spawn VanishOrMoveAside     WIPES silently (Addition 3)\n  DevVerbs.SpawnPawn             GenSpawn.Spawn + CellFinder fallback SLIDES silently (issue names it)\n  JournalVerbs (selftest pawn)   GenSpawn.Spawn @ RandomClosewalkCellNear(anchor,12)  deliberate scatter, no cell was requested — no change owed\n  JournalVerbs.SpawnPlayerBuilding GenSpawn.Spawn WipeMode.Vanish     callers site it via FindClearRect, which THROWS when no clear rect exists — guarded, no change owed\n  PawnFixtureVerbs.Prisoner      GenSpawn.Spawn @ RandomClosewalkCellNear(anchor,10)  deliberate scatter — no change owed\n  WorldFixtureVerbs.Bench        GenSpawn.Spawn WipeMode.Vanish @ FindClearRect.CenterCell  guarded — no change owed\n\n  (Grep used: `GenPlace|GenSpawn|ThingPlaceMode` over `Source/AutoRimmer/`.\n  Note that greping only those three names is what nearly hides `SpawnPawn`:\n  its slide is in `CellFinder.RandomClosewalkCellNear` on the line ABOVE the\n  `GenSpawn.Spawn`. A worker auditing by grep should also grep\n  `CellFinder.Random|TryFindRandomCellNear|Standable\\(`.)\n\nWHAT I AM INFERRING, NOT CONFIRMING\n\n- That `extraValidator: c =\u003e c == target` behaves as described end to end. I read\n  the call chain (`TryPlaceThing` -\u003e `TryFindPlaceSpotNear` -\u003e `PlaceSpotQualityAt`,\n  which returns `Unusable` when `extraValidator != null \u0026\u0026 !extraValidator(c)`),\n  but I did not run it. Worth one bench call to confirm before it becomes the\n  default.\n- The claim that a slide of more than one cell has ever been OBSERVED. It has\n  not, as far as I know; I am asserting the mechanism permits it, not that it\n  happened.","files":null}]}